          "ruleId": "review-note",
          "ruleIndex": 0,
          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "ms2v8f10szk3efpj",
          "message": {
            "text": "MAP is exported (and main() now runs only as an entry point) so the ticket-marker gate derives \"which docs are published\" from this file instead of keeping a second list.\n\nThe convention that 18 markers slipped past named a doc range (1-overview … 8-api-reference) that had since grown to 12 synced docs. Duplicating the list into the checker would reproduce exactly that failure mode. Importing MAP means a doc added to the sync map is covered automatically.\n\nThe entry-point guard is what makes the import side-effect-free — without it, importing this module would write all ten Starlight copies as a side effect of running the check.\n",
            "markdown": "`MAP` is exported (and `main()` now runs only as an entry point) so the ticket-marker gate derives \"which docs are published\" from this file instead of keeping a second list.\n\nThe convention that 18 markers slipped past named a doc range (`1-overview` … `8-api-reference`) that had since grown to 12 synced docs. Duplicating the list into the checker would reproduce exactly that failure mode. Importing `MAP` means a doc added to the sync map is covered automatically.\n\nThe entry-point guard is what makes the import side-effect-free — without it, importing this module would write all ten Starlight copies as a side effect of running the check.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "site/scripts/sync-docs.mjs"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 113,
                  "endLine": 115,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "// Only sync when run as a script. Importing this module (the ticket-marker\n// check imports `MAP`) must not write files as a side effect.\nif (process.argv[1] && resolve(process.argv[1]) === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) {"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
